<title>FRANCE: EU grants 22,500 tonnes oats exports.</title>
<headline>EU grants 22,500 tonnes oats exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted exports of 20,000 tonnes of oats to non-EU countries at a maximum refund of 29.94 Ecus per tonne and 2,500 tonnes to Switzerland at 29.25 Ecus, member state officials said.</p>
<p>They also confirmed wheat and barley exports reported earlier and added that rye and Greek maize exports had been rejected at a weekly tender.  </p>
<p>The previously reported exports were 398,500 tonnes of soft wheat at a maximum refund of 12.90 Ecus per tonne, and 145,700 tonnes of barley at a maximum refund of 27.49 Ecus per tonne.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
